  "narrative": "All returned estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so positive values support the corresponding claim. H80 receives the response-deadline reassessment for PTEN loss and dependency_STAT3 among high-screen-quality lines. Discovery R62 was +0.239 (95% interval +0.173 to +0.306), and independent validation R66 was +0.243 (independent interval +0.141 to +0.345). The signed positive estimate means PTEN-loss lines have a more negative dependency_STAT3 score, i.e. stronger STAT3 dependency. The validated effect remains large and precise; its lower bound is above even a conservative absolute 0.10 dependency-score benchmark and far above an approximate 10%-of-population-magnitude benchmark. I therefore accept and close H80. H112 tests TP53 loss and dependency_USP7 among KEAP1-loss co-loss lines, where the signed positive direction means TP53-loss lines have a less negative dependency_USP7 score, i.e. weaker USP7 dependency. Discovery R92 was +0.493 (interval +0.351 to +0.635), and independent validation R93 remained positive at +0.360 with adjusted interval +0.110 to +0.610. This supports the association in the KEAP1-loss co-loss context, although the point estimate is smaller than the full-population estimate and the validation interval is wider, consistent with smaller exposed and comparator cells. I accept and close H112. The dataset-specific supported core is now: SMARCA4 loss is associated with markedly stronger SMARCA2 dependency across the full population and many genomic/technical strata; TP53 loss is associated with markedly weaker USP7 dependency, including in KEAP1-loss co-loss lines; KEAP1 loss is associated with markedly weaker NFE2L2 dependency; MSI-high status is associated with markedly stronger WRN dependency; and PTEN loss is associated with markedly stronger STAT3 dependency across broad and high-quality contexts. Supported negative or unsupported areas include MSI-high-associated POLR2A dependency, PTEN-loss-associated KRAS-dependency changes among KRAS-mutant lines after failed validation, canonical TP53-loss MDM2 effects, and several small marker/co-driver screens. Unresolved uncertainty remains mainly around weak KRAS-co-driver signals and co-loss/technical interaction questions. The most informative next analyses are the newly registered refinements plus already active H113-H116: PTEN-loss/STAT3 in high-quality TP53-loss lines, TP53-loss/USP7 in high-quality KEAP1-loss lines, a KEAP1-loss interaction for TP53-loss/USP7 under high-quality screens, and SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 in high-quality ARID1A-loss co-loss lines. These remain observational associations in this supplied dataset only, not causal or externally generalizable claims."
